/-!
# S2031: the local realified monoid family of C^⊩env / C^⊩gau and the one-column carrier

Layer: O (original Theta-link / q-pilot).  Consumer of

* S1965 (the F^⊩-prime-strip carrier FDoublePlusPrimeStrip and the actual C-mod
  carrier paperModFDoublePlus),
* S1966 (the local theta/Gaussian monoid models LocalThetaMonoidModel and
  localGaussianValueMonoid),
* S1973 (the PsiEnv/PsiGau models, the evaluation psiEvaluation and its
  bijectivity, the unit and ray splittings),
* S1978 (the actual local O^× F-prime-strip on the one-column places).

## The paper statement

IUT II, Corollary 4.6, (v), constructs the global realified Frobenioids
C^env(†HT_Θ), C^gau(†HT_Θ) together with isomorphisms of topological monoids

  Φ_{C^env(†HT_Θ),v} ≅ Ψ^Fenv(†HT_Θ)^R_v,
  Φ_{C^gau(†HT_Θ),v} ≅ Ψ^Fgau(†HT_Θ)^R_v,          v ∈ V.

The superscript R is the realification of Corollary 4.5, (v): the local monoid
Ψ^env_v (respectively Ψ^gau_v) is replaced by the realification of the quotient
of its *ind-topological monoid portion* by its submonoid of units; the result is
the ray R_{≥0} generated by the distinguished element log(p_v) (respectively by
the Gaussian vector (..., j² log(p_v), ...)).  In the notation of Proposition
4.1, (iv), the local monoids are

  Ψ_env(Π_v) = Ψ_cns(Π_v)^× × R_{≥0}·log(p_v)·log(Θ),
  Ψ_gau(Π_v) = Ψ_cns(Π_v)^×⟨F_l⟩ × R_{≥0}·(..., j² log(p_v), ...),

and the evaluation isomorphism Ψ_env → Ψ_gau restricts to the identity on the
constant factor and sends log(p_v)log(Θ) to (..., j² log(p_v), ...).

## What is constructed here (kernel-checked)

1. **The realified local theta monoid at every one-column place**
   v : FinitePrimePlace 2 7:

     EnvRealified v := Multiplicative NNReal      (the ray R_{≥0}),

   with the realification map

     psiEnvRealification v : PsiEnvModel v →* Multiplicative NNReal,
     (u,c) ↦ c.

   It is surjective, kills the constant factor psiEnvUnitSection v, is the
   identity on the theta ray psiEnvRaySection v, sends the formal generator
   localThetaGenerator v (= log(p_v)log(Θ)) to the distinguished element 1, and
   satisfies the universal property psiEnvRealification_factors: every monoid
   hom killing the constant factor factors through it.  This is exactly the
   operator of Corollary 4.5, (v), on the S1966 model: the model's constant
   (ind-topological) portion is the actual local unit group
   (IndIntegralMonoid (Q_p))^×, a group, so the quotient by its unit group is
   trivial, and what remains is the theta ray, which is already the
   realification R_{≥0}.  The paper's full constant monoid Ψ_cns (which contains
   non-units) is not modeled by S1966/S1973 — that is their first missing — so
   the present model captures the unit portion of Ψ_cns; on that portion the
   realified quotient is trivial.

2. **The realified local Gaussian monoid and its identification with PsiGau.**
   psiEnvGauEquiv v l : PsiEnvModel v ≃* PsiGauModel v l is the bijective
   evaluation psiEvaluation v l, and

     psiGauRealification v l := psiEnvRealification v ∘ (psiEnvGauEquiv v l).symm.

   It is surjective, kills the constant factor, is the identity on the Gaussian
   ray, and satisfies the exact compatibility

     psiGauRealification v l (psiEvaluation v l z) = psiEnvRealification v z:

   the evaluation of Corollary 4.6, (iv), intertwines the two realifications
   with no normalization constant, because the distinguished element is 1 on
   both sides.

3. **The family package** LocalRealifiedFamily and the two actual families
   envLocalFamily, gauLocalFamily at the one-column places, together with the
   theta-model package LocalThetaModelFamily and its one-column realizations.

4. **The one-column C^⊩env / C^⊩gau carriers**

     oneColumnEnvDoublePlus : FDoublePlusPrimeStrip (FinitePrimePlace 2 7),
     oneColumnGauDoublePlus l : FDoublePlusPrimeStrip (FinitePrimePlace 2 7),

   built from
   * the actual one-column C-mod: the realified arithmetic Frobenioid of the
     rational base field, whose local divisor components at the one-column
     places are the actual v-components (≅ R_{≥0});
   * the actual local O^× F^†-strip of S1978;
   * the constructed local realified monoid family and its rho.
   The normalization is proved (oneColumnEnvDoublePlus_rho_prime): rho sends the
   prime generator of the local divisor component to the distinguished element
   1, the image of log(p_v)log(Θ) under the realification.

   This is the *one-column* carrier, over the rational base field whose places
   are exactly the one-column theta places.  It is not S1965's paperModFDoublePlus
   (which is the C-mod over Fmod), and no identification between the two is
   asserted.

## The exact first missing (reported, not faked)

The paper's C^env/C^gau are indexed by the place set V of the Θ-bridge, i.e. the
places of the base field Fmod = (S1895PaperInput.I D).initial.arithmetic.Fmod
(= ℚ(i) for the source data), not by the one-column index FinitePrimePlace 2 7.
Over the Fmod place set the carrier's local realified slots are *not* the
obstruction: the local realified monoid of C^env/C^gau is R_{≥0} at every place,
and the constant family (fun _ => Multiplicative NNReal) fills
FDoublePlusPrimeStrip exactly as in S1965 (paperConstantRealifiedCarrier is
literally paperModFDoublePlus).  What is missing is the *identification* of that
R_{≥0} with the realification of the paper's local theta/Gaussian monoid at each
place v of Fmod.  That requires

  (a) the local theta/Gaussian monoid at the completion F_v of Fmod at v,
      including the archimedean places v ∈ Varc (∞Ψ), with its action and
      splittings — S1966/S1973 construct the models only at the one-column
      rational primes (the local field Q_p), not at the places of Fmod;
  (b) the cohomological Ψ_cns construction of [AbsTopIII], Corollary 1.10, (b),
      which is the first missing object of S1966/S1973 and is not constructed
      here either;
  (c) the Θ-bridge gluing of Corollary 4.6, (iv), and the geometric F^† local
      components (the second boundary of S1965).

None of (a)-(c) is a place reindexing: the one-column index has four elements
(the rational primes 2,3,5,7), while the place set of Fmod is infinite, so no
equivalence exists; the datum is a per-place local monoid, not a relabeling of
the constructed one-column family.  FmodLocalThetaModel below records the
precise missing datum (a family over the Fmod places with the constant/ray
decomposition and the realification), with no inhabitant; no theorem consumes
it.  The one-column instance of the same package is inhabited by
envOneColumnThetaModelFamily and gauOneColumnThetaModelFamily l.

No sorry, axiom, True/PUnit slot, empty type or assumption-only Nonempty gate is
used.  The only classical inputs are those of the imported S1965/S1966/S1973/
S1978 files (propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound).
-/

